OPENSTREETMAP-DERIVED COORDINATES
---------------------------------

This one carries an obligation beyond CC BY, and it is not optional.

Ten of the fifteen sites in the register carry a coordinate recorded with
`coords_source: "osm"`. Those positions were checked against, and in places
taken from, OpenStreetMap. OpenStreetMap data is:

    © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open Database Licence
    (ODbL 1.0) — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Our CC BY 4.0 grant applies to our own compilation, description and
structure. It cannot and does not relicense OpenStreetMap's data. If you
extract the OSM-derived coordinates and build a database from them, ODbL's
attribution and share-alike terms apply to you regardless of anything in
this file.

Sites recorded with `coords_source: "doc"` are read from published documents
and are not OSM-derived. They are also not survey-grade, and they are
published as `surveyed: false` for exactly that reason.


